        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> > I was responsive, and there was an ongoing discussion in which you chose not to participate.\n> \n> I did replied, and that \"discussion\" totally irrelevant for the fix.\n> \n> You've been non-responsive for over a week, leaving config broken for most users. It's ok for adding new non-breaking feature, but your setup is rather niche, I'm not responsible for that.\n> \n> Please do prioritize the fix next time for the break you applied to most users.\n\nI don't think it's fair to characterize me as \"non-responsive\" simply because I didn't produce a fix within a week.\n\nThis is an open-source project, and a one-week response time for a bug report is not unreasonable, particularly when there was already an ongoing discussion about the underlying change. I did respond to that discussion; you may disagree with the direction of it, but that is different from being non-responsive.\n\nI'm glad the issue has now been resolved, but I would appreciate keeping the discussion factual and avoiding assumptions about other contributors' responsiveness or priorities.\n",
